**Read:** [Steels: Structure, Properties, and Design — Bhadeshia and Honeycombe](../sources/Steels-Structure-Properties-and-Design.lingua#r_5CB9R75MR8424M7VJ5Y33FY0QF), complete relevant surface-treatment and structure/property chapters, when available; [Ferrous Metals Processing Industry — European Commission BREF](../sources/Ferrous-Metals-Processing-BREF.lingua#r_49RSZE1MH5VHM49SDAXFQGHWRD), whole applicable surface preparation, coating, finishing, and utility/residual chapters; [Aluminium Automotive Manual — European Aluminium and collaborators](../sources/Aluminium-Automotive-Manual.lingua#r_73MPKA19MDBSQ96195B818Z49T), the complete relevant surface finishing and joining material; [Metals, alloys, steels, and graduate modeling — Bhadeshia teaching materials](../sources/Metals-Alloys-and-Graduate-Teaching-Bhadeshia.lingua#r_0HZJKN8WC6SEWA0DABM8P4HC3F), full diffusion, residual-stress, and surface-related discussions used.

Surface hardening, diffusion-based chemistry changes, coatings, and surface finishing modify different parts of a material. Composition/depth profiles, phase/defect changes, residual stress, interface adhesion, roughness, continuity, and thickness can affect wear, corrosion, fatigue, joining, and other uses. A surface hardness or coating label alone does not describe them all.

Use reaction/diffusion, thermal, deposition, and interface models with their actual boundary/history and material assumptions. A thin hard layer on an unsuitable substrate or an imperfectly bonded coating may not provide the intended performance. Local defects and processing-induced changes can control failure.

Compare the complete preparation, treatment, finishing, inspection, waste/water/gas, and maintenance account. A favorable isolated laboratory result may not transfer across geometry, batch, environment, load, or production variability. Match test evidence to the actual service question.

**Work:** reconstruct a full surface-treatment/coating study with chemistry, structure/depth, interface, and performance observations. Independently check a significant diffusion/thermal or material relation and compare with a competing damage/adhesion mechanism. Evaluate an alternative route on a defined function and test a changed service condition. Explain which observation would most change the interpretation and connect the result with the later failure-analysis study.

**Continue:** [Explain a joint through chemistry, heat, flow, transformations, and evidence across its regions](../manufacturing/Joining-weld-metallurgy-heat-affected-zones-and-dissimilar-materials.lingua#r_4D14X4AKXB4YK072HE2FCYD68A).

